ately, it exposes my hand and limits scoring potential. By passing, I maintain flexibility to form a more valuable concealed hand. With pairs of T5, T6, B5, and B7 already in hand, plus the existing T5-T6-T7 meld, I have multiple paths to winning with better scoring patterns like \"Concealed Hand\" (2 points) or \"All Chows\" (2 points). The unshown tiles suggest good drawing opportunities for T4 (3 left) to complete T4-T5-T6.\n\nAnswer: Pass"}
